New Playable Race: Drow
The drow - dark elves of the underdark - are now available as an advanced
playable race for accounts with at least one level-50 character.

Drow are a glass-cannon spellcaster race: high intelligence, dexterity,
and charisma offset by frail constitution and poor wisdom.  They have
infravision, are harder to spot indoors, and resist charm, paralysis,
and magical sleep.  Their racial pariah status follows them everywhere -
the cityguards of Grimhaven and Brightmoon attack drow PCs on sight,
and even their own kin in T'ir Na Z'goth are no friendlier.

A new 'innate' command surfaces racial activated abilities and their
cooldowns.  Drow get two: short-duration invisibility for slipping
past hostiles to reach a trainer, and a magical darkness that smothers
the current room and blinds any occupant lacking infravision or true
sight (including the drow themselves).  Each is usable about twice per
game day.

Note for elves: paralysis resistance has been adjusted from 50 to 40
as part of the racial balance pass.

See 'help drow' and 'help innate' for details.
